# NetworkManager owns networking on ShedOS. Without this, systemd's own
# 90-systemd.preset enables systemd-networkd at first boot (preset-all runs
# on a fresh machine-id), and its wait-online then times out on every boot —
# networkd manages no links here — leaving the system degraded. First match
# wins across preset files, so these lines shadow the systemd defaults.
disable systemd-networkd.service
disable systemd-networkd.socket
disable systemd-networkd-wait-online.service
